{
  "_comment": [
    "Measured on rbe-west, the lane's own remote executors (instance oss), on",
    "2026-10-09: two `bazel test --config=embedded --nocache_test_results",
    "//internal/storage/embeddeddolt:embeddeddolt_embedded_test` runs (race,",
    "`-test.parallel=4`), one with the then-committed 15-shard manifest and one",
    "with an 18-shard repack, so every one of the 395 top-level Test* functions",
    "(excluding TestConformance, sharded separately, and TestMain) ran exactly",
    "once per run. Each value is the mean of the two runs; the second ran under",
    "heavier executor load and came out ~25% slower across the board, which is",
    "the spread to expect between CI runs. Both runs were taken after",
    "RunBatchGetterAcceptsExactlyTheCap started seeding its 1000 issues in one",
    "CreateIssues call (TestBatchGetterContract: 198.87s -> ~7s on the same",
    "executors). The previous capture was local sandboxed execution, and it",
    "predated TestBatchGetterContract, so the packer weighted that test at its",
    "t.Run fallback (~54s) and stacked a ~200s test onto an already full shard",
    "(shard 9 of 15: 352s in CI). Remote shard wall time tracked the packed",
    "cost to within 2% in both runs (correlation 0.999+).",
    "",
    "Each value is that top-level test's own <testcase time=...> from Bazel's",
    "generated test.xml, NOT the enclosing <testsuite time=...>, for the same",
    "reason documented in scripts/ci/embedded_cmd_test_durations.json's header",
    "(empirically, <testsuite time> is a wall-clock-since-binary-start",
    "timestamp that does not isolate a concurrently-run top-level test's own",
    "duration under -test.parallel=4, while <testcase time> matches the test",
    "binary's own `--- PASS: TestX (Ys)` line exactly). Do not switch this",
    "capture to <testsuite time> without re-verifying that relationship for the",
    "toolchain in use at the time.",
    "",
    "One originally-measured top-level function,",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts_Embedded (350.25s: 81.03s + 260.70s +",
    "8.52s for its 356/712/classic-40 subtests), was subsequently split (same",
    "F1 CI-speed pass, see this file's git history) into 3 smaller",
    "top-level functions, one per shape:",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts356_Embedded,",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts712_Embedded and",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCountsClassic40_Embedded. Unlike the cmd",
    "tier's reconstructed split durations, these 3 have always been exact, not",
    "summed estimates: each runs exactly the one subtest the original combined",
    "function used to, and this file's values are now a direct, fresh",
    "per-function measurement from the same concurrent-load sweep as every",
    "other test in this file (not a reconstruction from an older, solo-measured",
    "capture). TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts712_Embedded genuinely still",
    "costs ~260-300s to actually run outside of -race (re-confirmed by a solo",
    "non-race re-measurement in an isolated clone: 298.60s) -- it is a single",
    "pinned statement-count assertion over one indivisible ApplyBatchInTx",
    "transaction (no internal sub-cases), so it cannot be split or shown to be",
    "a measurement artifact the way some of the cmd tier's flagged outliers",
    "were (see that file's header for the retraction of that theory -- it never",
    "applied here; this test's cost is real work, not scheduling).",
    "",
    "F1 follow-up (coordinator item 2): rather than leave this as the tier's",
    "irreducible ~260.7s floor, it is now skipped under raceEnabled (the exact",
    "precedent TestLargeBatchApplyWallClock_Embedded set for its 1000-item",
    "shape -- the cost is race-instrumentation overhead on the Dolt engine's",
    "own internal goroutine/lock machinery, not this test's own logic), with",
    "nightly.yml's \"Embedded Dolt batch-apply suite (non-race)\" step's -run",
    "regex extended to still run the full pinned assertion every night (and, as",
    "of this capture, given an explicit -timeout and `if: ${{ !cancelled() }}`",
    "so it still runs and reports even if an earlier nightly step fails). Its",
    "weight below is therefore set to 1.0 (negligible: a skipped subtest's own",
    "<testcase time> was observed at 0.00s in this capture too, confirming the",
    "skip is still in effect; 1.0 is a small nonzero placeholder so LPT packing",
    "still orders it after truly-free slots), reflecting what this test",
    "actually costs the per-PR -race lane bazel-embedded packs for -- NOT its",
    "real non-race cost, which is still ~260-300s and is what nightly.yml",
    "exercises. Do not revert this weight to 260.7 without also reverting the",
    "raceEnabled skip in large_batch_apply_measure_test.go -- the two must stay",
    "in sync.",
    "",
    "`seconds_per_init_fallback` is the weighted average seconds-per-init over",
    "every measured test in this file (sum of all durations / sum of all",
    "inits, where inits is discover_inits_cost()'s t.Run( count proxy), used",
    "only for a brand-new test with no entry yet (see",
    "scripts/ci/gen_embedded_storage_shard_manifest.py's discover_inits_cost()).",
    "",
    "As with the proxied and cmd tiers' duration files, these are a relative",
    "weight for LPT bin-packing, not an absolute SLA: within-shard",
    "-test.parallel=4 overlap, farm noisy-neighbor effects, and future code",
    "changes all mean a shard's total packed cost is a planning estimate, not",
    "a guarantee."
  ],
